name: Honest engine maturity, dependency presence and missing-model readiness
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN SEMGREP_AGENT_TOKEN
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/engine_readiness.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
submit: run context:build {"enrichment":false}
require-live-snap: 35 context:build indexed | source-indexed
submit: use sast
submit: options sast:scan
submit: setg taskMode manual
submit: setg tasks semgrep
paste-file: @ART/binary-setting.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/engine_readiness.py @TMP_TARGET @ART globals
submit: scan batch
require-live-snap: 25 PLAN A STUDY | study
keys: Home Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 25 DEPENDENCY MISSING: semgrepBinary | missing-executable
expect: r check
expect: [x] semgrep
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 15 DEPENDENCY MISSING: semgrepBinary | missing-executable-40x12
expect: r check
resize: 120x36
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/engine_readiness.py @TMP_TARGET @ART nonexecutable
keys: r
require-live-snap: 20 DEPENDENCY MISSING: semgrepBinary | nonexecutable
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/engine_readiness.py @TMP_TARGET @ART executable
keys: r
require-live-snap: 20 Executable found (presence only) | presence-only
expect: CHECKS PENDING
ask: Does missing and nonexecutable input become only a presence result after explicit recheck, without implying scanner compatibility or starting work?
keys: Down
require-live-snap: 20 [Labs] codeql | experimental-codeql
expect: Experimental (Labs)
expect: No database is created here.
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 15 [Labs] codeql | experimental-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 15 [Labs] codeql | experimental-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 15 [Labs] codeql | experimental-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 15 [Labs] codeql | experimental-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 15 [Labs] codeql | experimental-40x12
expect: r check
keys: NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage
require-live-snap: 15 guarantee. | detail-tail-40x12
ask: Is experimental status visible at all six sizes, with scope, pending checks, apply, cancel and presence recheck understandable and complete details reachable at 40 columns?
resize: 120x36
keys: Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Down
require-live-snap: 20 offense-review:threat-hunt | model-prerequisite
expect: PREREQUISITE MISSING
expect: Experimental (Labs)
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 15 PREREQUISITE MISSING | model-prerequisite-40x12
expect: model required
resize: 120x36
keys: Space
require-live-snap: 20 [x] [Labs] offense-review | explicit-experimental-draft
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 Discovery engines  current settings | canceled-draft
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/engine_readiness.py @TMP_TARGET @ART cancelled
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 [x] semgrep | restored-selection
keys: Escape
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/engine_readiness.py @TMP_TARGET @ART complete
ask: Does a missing model remain a prerequisite, with experimental choices requiring explicit selection and Cancel preserving the original study and globals without approving any jobs or model requests?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | no-color-restart
submit: scan batch
require-live-snap: 25 PLAN A STUDY | restarted-study
keys: Home Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Executable found (presence only) | restarted-presence
expect: [x] semgrep
keys: Down
require-live-snap: 20 [Labs] codeql | restarted-experimental
expect: Experimental (Labs)
keys: Escape
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/engine_readiness.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain the original engine and dependency setting, recheck presence honestly, and preserve experimental labels without creating a plan or spending?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
